"<strong>Q6.</strong> Why does a {#} km planetesimal formed at {#} million years stay cool, while a {#} km one formed at the same time melts?",
"<strong>\"The planets formed in order outward from the Sun, as the disk cooled.\"</strong> The disk had its temperature profile all at once; what differs with distance is what can be solid and how fast bodies grow.",
"<strong>\"The Sun's gravity flattens the disk.\"</strong> Gravity alone would pull everything in; it is the spin, kept as the cloud shrinks, together with the collisions of gas falling from above and below, that makes a flat disk.",
"<strong>\"The giant planets are big because they are far away.\"</strong> They are big because beyond the frost line there was more solid material, so their cores reached the size needed to pull in gas before the gas disappeared.",
