"<strong>Collapse.</strong> The infall model of Ulrich ({#}, ApJ {#}, {#}): parcels fall freely in the pull of the young Sun, as if its mass were already at the center, from a cloud turning as one body. A parcel starting at radius r₀ and distance s from the axis crosses the midplane at the semi latus rectum of its orbit, (Ω₀ s r₀)²/GM, whatever its energy (checked in the tests). There its up and down motion is removed (gas from above meets gas from below), its spin about the axis j_z = Ω₀ s² is kept, and its motion toward or away from the Sun dies out over about an orbit, so it settles at j_z²/GM. The disk's edge is R_d = Ω₀² r₀⁴/GM. Parcels that would come within {#} AU join the Sun. The cloud's own gravity and pressure, magnetic braking and the disk's later spreading are left out. The default spin, once every {#} million years ({#} × {#}⁻¹⁴ s⁻¹), is within the range measured in dense cores (Goodman et al. {#}).",
